<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Srinagar, Uttarakhand</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srinagar">Srinagar</a> is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaknanda">Alaknanda</a> River in Pauri <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garhwal">Garhwal</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttarakhand">Uttarakhand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parmar-rajputs">Panwar</a> kings of Garhwal from the 16th century until the Gorkha conquest of 1804, after which the restored dynasty moved to Tehri. It lies on the pilgrim route to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badrinath">Badrinath</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kedarnath">Kedarnath</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/srinagar-uttarakhand.jpg" alt="Srinagar, Uttarakhand" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shubham Semwal · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Srinagar_Garhwal_with_Chauras_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
